Marguerite, ahead of closing, our process on payment instructions, because it=
 is the one thing that reliably causes a problem late.

We do not accept or act on payment instructions received by email, including =
from a known contact, and including where the email appears to be part of an =
existing thread. Instructions must come through the portal with dual authoriz=
ation from two of your registered signatories.

Changes to previously registered instructions require a callback to a number =
we hold on file rather than a number provided in the request. We will make th=
at call and we will not proceed without completing it.

None of this is a comment on your controls. It is the same process for every =
client and it exists because the failure mode is expensive and irreversible. =
Please build the callback into your closing timetable rather than treating it=
 as a formality.

